@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title Four acts, four kinds of state, one arrow each — and no arrow anywhere else

rectangle "COMMIT" as C #f6fbfa
rectangle "PROMOTE" as P #f6fbfa
rectangle "BUILD" as B #f6fbfa
rectangle "DEPLOY" as D #f6fbfa

database "the repository\nwhat the firm has written" as REPO
database "the branch pointers\nwhich commit each environment is at" as PTR
database "the build output\none directory per target per package" as OUT
database "the running target\nwhat is actually serving" as RUN

C -down-> REPO : writes
P -down-> PTR  : advances, one step
B -down-> OUT  : writes
D -down-> RUN  : installs

note right of C
  Refuses: anything failing a rule; anything
  without an authorisation given at that moment;
  any branch but dev.
  The commit is all-or-nothing: if ONE file
  fails a rule, the ENTIRE commit fails.
  Does NOT touch the running target.
end note

note right of P
  Refuses: a skipped step, a partial tree.
  Does NOT build and does NOT deploy.
  It moves a pointer and nothing else.
end note

note right of B
  Reads the working tree for local, the
  environment's branch otherwise.
  Refuses a declared file not on disk.
  Does NOT reach any environment.
end note

note right of D
  Reads ONLY the build output, never source.
  Refuses a target that does not report the
  build it was given.
end note

note as ABSENCE #fff4e5
  The absences are the subject.

  There is no arrow from source to a running target and
  no arrow from a commit to an environment. These four
  acts govern CODE only.

  Data reaches a served store by ONE further governed
  act -- a data migration (EPIC-010-F-108): human-released,
  server-side, moving a published generation from the
  pipeline cluster to the served cluster under its own
  name. It is governed by the Data Architecture chapter,
  NOT by this chain. It is a sanctioned separate path,
  not a fifth code act -- so it is not one of the defects
  below.

  Every OTHER path that reaches a remote system is outside
  this model. The firm found such paths existed -- hand
  edits to Azure, Atlas, Key Vault, runbooks -- and no gate
  objected, because every gate asks whether what SHIPS is
  declared and none asks whether what RUNS is. That reverse
  direction is BUG-008 and is still open (N32, N38, N56).
end note

@enduml
